<title>BELGIUM: Ministers update beef and pork control system.</title>
<headline>Ministers update beef and pork control system.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm ministers adopted by qualified majority on Monday, without discussion, a proposal to update and simplify health checks on cattle and pigs traded between EU member states, a statement said.</p>
<p>Britain, Germany and Sweden voted against the updating of Directive 432/64, which has already been modified 40 times, and to set up a system of regular inspections and disease surveillance.</p>
<p>It includes the creation of EU-wide computerised cattle and pig data bases which would lay the basis for a proposed cattle identification system to help control bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE).</p>
</text>
